{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/530926-character-conversion-to-requiem-2-0","id":530926,"title":"Character Conversion to Requiem 2.0?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-28T06:38:04-07:00","id":530926,"title":"Character Conversion to Requiem 2.0?","content":"Hi all,<br /> <br /> sorry if it has been asked before, I couldn't find any relevant info.<br /> A few years back I ran a Requiem campaign for my group, then it slowly ended in the middle of the things. <br /> I just found out about the second edition and I'm intrigued to give it a try and as far as I can tell without purchasing<br /> and reading the core book, it would be more attractive to my players then the first edition because of the changes<br /> that were made. My question is: is there an easy way to convert the characters from the first ed to the second<br /> and pick up the story? Or is it a blasphemy even considering it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> I know it could raise some continuity problems but we just want to have some fun. <br /> thanks for your help, guys","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6179-wmute","name":"wmute","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T06:49:25-07:00","id":530950,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think you should be ok. Depends on what exactly the characters could do, really. Some of the disciplines got off more intact than others (some of the powers are devotions now) and the coils of the dragon are a bit different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T07:33:15-07:00","id":530995,"title":"","content":"Converting characters is very easy, in my experience. There are basically two ways you can go about it:<br /> <br /> 1. Direct port. Simply put the exact same dots into everything on a 2e character sheet. As Elfive pointed out, there are a few things like Coils, Devotions, and some Merits that don't line up perfectly, so you'll have to fudge things here and there, but this method *mostly* works, and keeps the 2e version of the character as close as possible to the 1e version. I usually prefer this method for NPCs.<br /> <br /> 2. Re-build under the new rules. Calculate how many experience points the character was built with, divide by five, and re-build the character from the ground up under the new rules with that many starting experiences (one 2e experience is roughly equivalent to five 1e experience). This method is a bit more involved and may lead to slightly different dot totals but has the benefit of ending up with &quot;what my character *would have* looked like if we had been playing 2e all along&quot; which may be more satisfying for the players. I usually prefer this method for PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-28-2015, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T08:08:55-07:00","id":531020,"title":"","content":"I had a Requiem for Rome chronicle that we converted to second edition about 3/4s of the way through. We just left the dots as they were, and adjusted for a few Merits. It was a fairly smooth transition, though we'd already been using the preview disciplines that'd been posted on the old website.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T12:59:58-07:00","id":531215,"title":"","content":"Besides the updated rules, reworked Disciplines and clan weaknesses and so on, a major feature of the new edition is Touchstones. They're not essential, characters can function without the, but they shift the focus of the game if they're there. Do your characters have anyone appropriate for the role? If not, perhaps they could gain them in the downtime between &quot;seasons&quot;, or could start the new run without them - maybe they've moved to a new city between runs and have fewer close connections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T00:14:39-07:00","id":531764,"title":"","content":"Thank you all for your input.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6179-wmute","name":"wmute","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T11:22:26-07:00","id":532085,"title":"","content":"I converted mid way through a game too. We added up all our experiences spent and Divided by 5 then re purchased everything. 5/6 of us ended up with more than what we had one of us lost out on stuff so we just let him direct port. <br /> <br /> however a direct port over screws people over if they started dumping all their exp into humanity or BP vs a person who bought skills and merits. <br /> <br /> it's super easy to just add the touchstone (most players in my experience, had something close to it anyway written into their stories ) 3 new merit dots, and the new mask and dirge.<br /> <br /> Our group was much happier after the conversion and never went back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}